  "body": {
    "id": "prop:rank-one-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "When \\(r=1\\) and \\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{causal}}(\\theta)\\ne\\varnothing\\), the sharp fiber reduces to \\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{causal}}(\\theta)=\\{\\{j\\}:Q_{jj}>0\\}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "r",
      "Fcausal",
      "theta",
      "Q"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:sharp-target-fiber"
    ],
    "justification": "This reduction checks that the multivariate certificate collapses to the known rank-one changing-column ambiguity.",
    "gap": "The rank-one case is implicit in covariance-factor arguments, but is stated here as the required sanity reduction of the general labeled-fiber theorem.",
    "consumer": "Practitioners with single effective perturbations obtain a closed-form candidate list without running the recursion.",
    "proof_tex": "Assume \\(r=1\\) and \\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{causal}}(\\theta)\\ne\\varnothing\\).  The sharp-fiber theorem gives a certified singleton \\(\\{k\\}\\).  Its realization, or equivalently range reconstruction applied to its certificate, shows that\n\\(Q=aa^{\\mathsf T}d\\) for some \\(d>0\\); hence \\(Q\\) is positive semidefinite of rank one.  For every \\(e\\), symmetry and\n\\(\\operatorname{range}(\\Delta_e)\\subseteq\\operatorname{range}(Q)=\\operatorname{span}\\{a\\}\\) imply\n\\(\\Delta_e=c_eQ\\) for a scalar \\(c_e\\).  At the certified coordinate \\(k\\), the scalar certificate equals\n\\(\\Delta_{e,kk}/Q_{kk}=c_e\\), so nonnegativity of that certificate gives \\(c_e\\ge0\\).\n\nNow fix any label \\(j\\).  For the one-element order \\(t=(j)\\), the reference block is the scalar \\(Q_{jj}\\).  It is positive exactly when \\(Q_{jj}>0\\); in that case its unit-lower factor is \\(L_t=(1)\\), and every transformed block is the scalar\n\\[\n \\Lambda_{e,t}=\\Delta_{e,jj}=c_eQ_{jj}\\ge0.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\{j\\}\\) is certified exactly when \\(Q_{jj}>0\\).  Applying the sharp-fiber equality proves\n\\(\\mathcal F_{\\mathrm{causal}}(\\theta)=\\{\\{j\\}:Q_{jj}>0\\}\\).",
